/// `sender.flow_control_receivers_timed_out`, a static counter: Receivers dropped from a min publication's table for no status message within the flow control receiver timeout, 5 s; one dropped because its last status message carried end of stream, as every receiver's does after a clean close, is not counted; the sender limit then follows the slowest of the receivers that remain (spec/udp.md, The sender; ADR 0053, ADR 0054).
pub const SENDER_FLOW_CONTROL_RECEIVERS_TIMED_OUT: CounterId = CounterId(101);

/// `sender.flow_control_receivers_full`, a static counter: Status messages from a receiver a min publication's full table of 64 does not hold: accepted for the connection and not tracked, so the sender limit does not follow that receiver (spec/udp.md, The sender; ADR 0053).
pub const SENDER_FLOW_CONTROL_RECEIVERS_FULL: CounterId = CounterId(102);

/// `sender.flow_control_receivers`, a instance gauge: The receivers in one cavalry:udp publication's min table, each answering within the flow control receiver timeout, and once the publication is closed each whose stream ended too, kept until the linger ends, so that a clean close leaves it at the receivers that took the stream to its end; 0 under max, which keeps no table; key as sender.position; label text: sender.position's four, then the publication's strategy as fc=max or fc=min, space-separated, so that doctor reads which publications keep a table (ADR 0053, ADR 0056).
pub const SENDER_FLOW_CONTROL_RECEIVERS: CounterId = CounterId(103);

/// `channel.destinations`, a instance gauge: How many destinations one send endpoint of a control channel sends to, added with add destination and removed with remove destination; 0 on any other endpoint; key and label as channel.status (spec/udp.md, The sender; ADR 0053).
pub const CHANNEL_DESTINATIONS: CounterId = CounterId(104);

/// `recording.armed`, a static counter: Start recording commands on a cavalry:udp stream with a live subscription and no live publication or image, answered with operation success and held as an armed recording, at most one per receive endpoint and stream with a live subscription, so the subscriptions registry bounds them, until the stream's next image arrives or its last subscription on the endpoint goes; each ends in one of recording.armed_started, recording.armed_failed and recording.armed_dropped, so this counter less those three is the recordings armed or starting (spec/client-protocol.md, Commands, start recording; ADR 0059).
pub const RECORDING_ARMED: CounterId = CounterId(105);

/// `recording.armed_started`, a static counter: Armed recordings that started when the stream's next image arrived, at the image's join position, before the image was announced, recording ready sent to the arming client with the arming command's correlation id, the command's second answer after its operation success (spec/client-protocol.md, Commands, start recording; ADR 0059).
pub const RECORDING_ARMED_STARTED: CounterId = CounterId(106);

/// `recording.armed_dropped`, a static counter: Armed recordings dropped because the last subscription on their receive endpoint and stream went before an image arrived, by remove subscription, client close or client timeout, a receive endpoint that closes being one case of it, since the receiver creates no image for a stream no subscription wants; the arming command is answered a second time with error code 20 (spec/client-protocol.md, Commands, start recording; ADR 0059).
pub const RECORDING_ARMED_DROPPED: CounterId = CounterId(107);

/// `recording.armed_failed`, a static counter: Armed recordings whose start failed when the stream's next image arrived, at a step a start on a live image fails at: the recordings registry, the recorder's request queue, the catalog or the counters file at capacity (code 10), or the recording's files not created (code 12). Each also counts in that step's counter, driver.registry_full, recording.catalog_full or recording.start_failed; the arming command is answered a second time with error and the code, and the image is announced all the same and no longer held by the recording (spec/client-protocol.md, Commands, start recording; ADR 0059).
pub const RECORDING_ARMED_FAILED: CounterId = CounterId(108);

/// `cluster.commit_position`, a client gauge: The commit position one cluster member knows: the position the leader has found a quorum has appended, which never falls; an entry at or below it is committed and a service reads nothing above it (spec/cluster.md, The log). The member's consensus module adds the counter and stores the value with a release store; a service loads it with an acquire load before it polls the log; key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_COMMIT_POSITION: CounterId = CounterId(109);

/// `cluster.elections`, a client counter: Elections one cluster member began, from init: on starting, and each time it begins again after a failed or lost election (spec/cluster.md, Roles and the election). At most one more than cluster.elections_closed and cluster.elections_failed together, the one more being the election under way; key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_ELECTIONS: CounterId = CounterId(110);

/// `cluster.terms_led`, a client counter: Terms one cluster member began to lead, on entering leader log replication: cluster.role going to leader (spec/cluster.md, Roles and the election); key and label as cluster.elections.
pub const CLUSTER_TERMS_LED: CounterId = CounterId(111);

/// `cluster.leader_quorum_losses`, a client counter: Times the active members of one cluster leader fell below a quorum, a member being active while its last report is younger than the leader heartbeat timeout, 10 s; the leader holds an election, beginning at init, a failed election when it was in leader log replication or leader ready (spec/cluster.md, The commit position; ADR 0082); key and label as cluster.elections.
pub const CLUSTER_LEADER_QUORUM_LOSSES: CounterId = CounterId(112);

/// `cluster.appointed_leader_behind`, a client counter: Members an appointed leader found holding a log ahead of its own, in canvass or in leader ready, once for each such member in an election. No member of this version counts it or adds it: a member elects its leader. It stays registered while cavalry doctor reads it, and leaves with that check (ADR 0100); key and label as cluster.elections.
pub const CLUSTER_APPOINTED_LEADER_BEHIND: CounterId = CounterId(113);

/// `cluster.log_images_lost`, a client counter: Times one cluster follower's image of its leader's log was no longer available, so that it began its election again at init (spec/cluster.md, Roles and the election); key and label as cluster.elections.
pub const CLUSTER_LOG_IMAGES_LOST: CounterId = CounterId(114);

/// `cluster.elections_failed`, a client counter: Elections one cluster member failed in a state and began again at init: a new leadership term from a leader whose log does not reach the member's position, a truncation below the commit position the member knows, an image of the log or of a replay that joined at another position, or a step that made no progress for the leader heartbeat timeout, 10 s; and, for a leader in leader log replication or leader ready, a canvass position with a term above its own or active members that fell below a quorum (spec/cluster.md, Roles and the election; ADR 0082, ADR 0083); key and label as cluster.elections.
pub const CLUSTER_ELECTIONS_FAILED: CounterId = CounterId(115);

/// `cluster.leader_heartbeat_timeouts`, a client counter: Times one cluster follower heard nothing from its leader for the leader heartbeat timeout, 10 s, and began its election again at init (spec/cluster.md, Roles and the election); key and label as cluster.elections.
pub const CLUSTER_LEADER_HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUTS: CounterId = CounterId(116);

/// `cluster.leadership_terms_ignored`, a client counter: New leadership term messages one cluster member ignored for their term: below its candidate term in canvass, or not the term it follows once it has taken a leader (spec/cluster.md, Messages during an election); key and label as cluster.elections.
pub const CLUSTER_LEADERSHIP_TERMS_IGNORED: CounterId = CounterId(117);

/// `cluster.join_position_mismatches`, a client counter: Images of the log that joined one cluster member somewhere other than where its log ends, so that it failed its election and left the image: in follower log await, state 15, an image of the live log that joined at a position other than its append position; in follower log replication, state 9, an image of a replay that joined at a position other than the one the member asked from; in follower catch-up await, state 12, the image of a catch-up's replay that joined at a position other than the one the member asked from (spec/cluster.md, Roles and the election, states 9, 12 and 15; ADR 0086, ADR 0088, ADR 0092); key and label as cluster.elections.
pub const CLUSTER_JOIN_POSITION_MISMATCHES: CounterId = CounterId(118);

/// `cluster.election_steps`, a client counter: Steps of one cluster member's election from one state to the next that neither begin it, fail it, close it nor make the member a leader: canvass to follower replay, follower replay to follower log init, follower log init to follower log await, follower log await to follower ready, leader log replication to leader replay, leader replay to leader init and leader init to leader ready (ADR 0067); and canvass to nominate, and nominate, candidate ballot and follower ballot to follower replay, a candidate's step to follower replay also moving cluster.role from candidate to follower (ADR 0081); and canvass, nominate, candidate ballot and follower ballot to follower log replication, a candidate's step there moving cluster.role as its step to follower replay does, and follower log replication to canvass (ADR 0086); and follower replay to follower catch-up init, follower catch-up init to follower catch-up await, follower catch-up await to follower catch-up, follower catch-up to follower log init, and follower log init to follower ready for a member the catch-up left subscribed (ADR 0088) (spec/cluster.md, Counters). With no ballot lost, no term replicated and no catch-up, an election that closes makes four on its leader, three on the leader of a cluster of one member, which leads from init, and four or five on a follower, five when the follower went through nominate; a member that nominates itself again after a ballot lost counts canvass to nominate again. A member that replicates a term it missed counts, for each such term, the step into follower log replication, canvass to nominate before it when it went through nominate, and the step back to canvass; then it counts the steps of the path it closes its election on from canvass, as above. So a follower that replicates one term and then joins counts at least six. A follower that joins its leader's term behind the leader's log catches up: from follower replay it counts five steps to follower ready, through the three states of the catch-up and follower log init, where a follower level with its leader counts three, so its election counts two more; key and label as cluster.elections.
pub const CLUSTER_ELECTION_STEPS: CounterId = CounterId(119);

/// `cluster.elections_closed`, a client counter: Elections one cluster member closed: leader ready to closed, its term's first entry appended, or follower ready to closed, its append position sent to its leader (spec/cluster.md, Counters; ADR 0067); key and label as cluster.elections.
pub const CLUSTER_ELECTIONS_CLOSED: CounterId = CounterId(120);

/// `cluster.role`, a client gauge: One cluster member's role: 0 follower, 1 candidate, 2 leader (spec/cluster.md, Counters). The member's consensus module adds the counter and stores it; key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_ROLE: CounterId = CounterId(121);

/// `cluster.election_state`, a client gauge: The state of one cluster member's election, the code spec/cluster.md, Roles and the election, gives it, 17 when no election runs; key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_ELECTION_STATE: CounterId = CounterId(122);

/// `cluster.leadership_term_id`, a client gauge: The term one cluster member leads or follows, -1 before the first; key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_LEADERSHIP_TERM_ID: CounterId = CounterId(123);

/// `cluster.append_position`, a client gauge: One cluster member's append position: the end of the contiguous span its recordings of the log hold, as a sync has made it durable (spec/cluster.md, The log; ADR 0060); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_APPEND_POSITION: CounterId = CounterId(124);

/// `cluster.messages_rejected`, a client counter: Messages of the consensus stream one cluster member rejected, for any reason of spec/cluster.md, What a reader rejects; key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_MESSAGES_REJECTED: CounterId = CounterId(125);

/// `cluster.log_recording_id`, a client gauge: The id of the recording one cluster member records the live log into, -1 while it records none: the leader's recording of its log publication, or a follower's recording of the leader's image it joined last; the recording its service replays (spec/cluster.md, The service; ADR 0066). The member's consensus module adds the counter and stores -1 in it before it adds cluster.commit_position, and stores a new value in it before it stores a commit position the recording does not hold; key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_LOG_RECORDING_ID: CounterId = CounterId(126);

/// `cluster.candidacies`, a client counter: Ballots one cluster member began as a candidate: it stored candidate term + 1, voted for itself and asked every other member for its vote, going from nominate to candidate ballot (spec/cluster.md, Roles and the election, state 3; ADR 0081); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
