pub const CLUSTER_LEADER_STEP_DOWNS: CounterId = CounterId(131);

/// `cluster.higher_terms_seen`, a client counter: Times one cluster follower whose election had closed held an election, beginning at init, on a term above its own: a request vote whose candidate term id or a commit position whose leadership term id above its leadership term id, from another member. The cluster began that term without it, and it joins it through the election it holds (spec/cluster.md, Messages outside an election, and Counters; ADR 0082); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_HIGHER_TERMS_SEEN: CounterId = CounterId(132);

/// `cluster.log_truncations`, a client counter: Times one cluster member truncated its log to join a leader: a new leadership term named, as the term its leader's record holds next after the member's own, a term whose base lay below the member's append position, and the member cut what it held above that base, with every term it had recorded above it. What it cut is the tail of an older term that no quorum recorded; a committed entry is never cut, and a member told to cut below the commit position it knows refuses and fails its election (spec/cluster.md, Messages during an election, and Counters; ADR 0083); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_LOG_TRUNCATIONS: CounterId = CounterId(133);

/// `cluster.truncations_refused`, a client counter: Times one cluster member was told, by a new leadership term, to truncate its log to a position below the commit position it knows, and did not: it kept its log and failed its election, counted in cluster.elections_failed too. A committed entry is never truncated, and a leader that holds what was committed names no such position (spec/cluster.md, Messages during an election, and Counters; ADR 0083); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_TRUNCATIONS_REFUSED: CounterId = CounterId(134);

/// `cluster.log_replications`, a client counter: Times one cluster member replicated, or served, a span of the log below the leader's term base log position, a term the member missed: on a follower, a catch-up position it sent from follower log replication, one for each replay it asked for; on the leader, a replay of its own recordings that it started for such a member, once for each replay where the span lies in several recordings (spec/cluster.md, follower log replication, Messages outside an election, and Counters; ADR 0085, ADR 0086, ADR 0092); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_LOG_REPLICATIONS: CounterId = CounterId(135);

/// `cluster.log_replications_unavailable`, a client counter: Times one cluster member failed its election in follower log replication because its append position stayed below its stop position without moving for the leader heartbeat timeout: the leader's recordings do not hold the span, purged by retention, a replay stopped for a fault, or the replay never reached the member's catchup endpoint. Counted in cluster.elections_failed too (spec/cluster.md, follower log replication, and Counters; ADR 0086); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_LOG_REPLICATIONS_UNAVAILABLE: CounterId = CounterId(136);

/// `cluster.catchups`, a client counter: Times one cluster member began, or served, a catch-up within the leader's term: on a follower, a catch-up position it sent from follower catch-up init; on the leader, a replay of its live recording that it started for such a member, which follows the recording until the leader stops it (spec/cluster.md, follower catch-up init, Messages outside an election, and Counters; ADR 0087, ADR 0088); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_CATCHUPS: CounterId = CounterId(137);

/// `cluster.terms_dropped`, a client counter: Times one cluster member dropped from its record of terms the terms its leader's record lacks: a new leadership term named, as the term it answers, a term below the member's own log term, with a next term above it, so the leader's record holds none of the member's terms above the one named, and the member took them out of its record, cutting first what it held above the base of the lowest of them, which is counted in cluster.log_truncations too (spec/cluster.md, Messages during an election, and Counters; ADR 0096); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_TERMS_DROPPED: CounterId = CounterId(138);

/// `cluster.leader_member_id`, a client gauge: The id of the member one cluster member leads as or follows, -1 while it has none: from init until it leads a term or takes a leader's new leadership term, so through canvass, nominate and the two ballots (spec/cluster.md, Counters; ADR 0077, ADR 0102); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
pub const CLUSTER_LEADER_MEMBER_ID: CounterId = CounterId(140);

/// `cluster.election_cause`, a client gauge: Why one cluster member's last election began, the election it is in or the one that closed last: 0 the member started; 1 it followed and its leader said nothing for the leader heartbeat timeout; 2 it followed and its image of the leader's log was no longer available; 3 it led and its active members fell below a quorum; 4 its election had closed and a message carried a term above its own; 5 its election before failed (spec/cluster.md, Counters; ADR 0077, ADR 0102); key: member id (i32), little-endian; label text: the member id in decimal.
